# Next.js web conventions

## Data fetching

All API calls go through `@questorylabs/qhttp` (`lib/qhttp-client.ts`, domain wrappers `api`/`musicFetch`/`watchFetch`/`readFetch`, `auth-api`, `enterprise-api`) with `@questorylabs/qhttp/react` (`useResource`/`useAction`/`useLiveResource`/`useStore`). Never call raw `fetch()` in components. For live data use `useLiveResource` (or the thin `useSseBackedQuery` wrapper), not polling loops.

**Loading UX:** full-page gates use `LoadingPage` + quotes. In-page resources use `ResourceStatus` from `@questorylabs/ui` with qHttp flags, **failed before empty**:

- `resource.failed` → `StateMessage variant="error"` or danger `EmptyState`
- `resource.empty` → first-load `Skeleton*`
- ready (`!empty && !failed`) → content, or collection `EmptyState` when the value has no items
- `resource.refreshing` → keep showing data; optional refreshing hint
- `resource.busy` is **not** the first-load gate (that is `empty`). `useAction.busy` / `useAction.failed` gate mutation buttons and errors.

Do not wait on every resource before painting the page — each section owns its own resource.

## Types come from shared

API response/request shapes are `import type { X } from "@questorylabs/shared"`. Do not re-declare local interfaces for API payloads (`AppShell`'s local `MeResponse` instead of the shared user schema is the anti-pattern — don't copy it). If a shape is missing from shared, add it there.

## Feature gating

Soft-gated routes (`/music/*`, `/watch/*`, `/read/*`, `/recommendations`, `/admin/telemetry`) are gated by the existing components/hooks: `MusicGate`, `WatchGate`, `ReadGate`, `EnterpriseGate` in layouts, and `useMusicEnabled`/`useWatchEnabled`/`useReadEnabled`/`useEnterpriseEnabled` for conditional UI. Never read feature-flag env vars or `/health` flags inline in a page.

## Components and pages

Authenticated routes use controller + view:

```
app/(app)/<route>/page.tsx          # compose only
  └── <Feature>Controller           # useResource / useAction / useState → cloneElements
        └── <Feature>View           # presentational; ResourceStatus per section
```

Files live in `apps/web/src/modules/<domain>/<feature>/` as `<domain>.<feature>.controller.tsx` / `.view.tsx`, plus optional `.hooks.tsx`, `.types.ts`, `.constants.ts`, `.utils.ts`. Omit empty stubs. Prefer `const` arrows over `function` declarations in new and moved files.

**Component placement**

- Primitives (no domain knowledge) → `@questorylabs/ui` (`Button`, `Dialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Panel`, `ResourceStatus`, `StateMessage`, `QMark`, skeletons). `components/ui` re-exports them; `StateMessage` there only injects the loading quote.
- Shared by two or more features → `apps/web/src/components/` (optionally `components/<domain>/`).
- One feature only → `modules/<domain>/<feature>/components/`. Promote to global `components/` if a second feature needs it; do not duplicate.

Reuse primitives first. Do not put `GameTile` / `StatCard` in the UI package.

A `page.tsx` only composes Controller + View — keep it tiny. Fat settings pages are the anti-pattern; extract sections into feature components.

Before building a music/watch/read variant of an existing component (pickers, insights charts, detail pages), generalize the existing one and parameterize the domain — do not add another near-identical copy.

Feature-local hooks, types, and constants colocate in the module. App-wide hooks (`useUser`, `useSyncJobs`) stay in `src/hooks/`. Shared API types stay in `@questorylabs/shared`. Page sizes stay in `lib/pagination.ts`.

## Destructive actions require confirmation

Any action that deletes, overwrites, re-runs, or otherwise mutates existing data (delete user, run/retry a migration, trigger a sync that rewrites imports, discard a draft) must show a confirmation step before the action fires. Use `Dialog` from `@questorylabs/ui` (re-exported from `components/ui`) with a Cancel + confirm button pair — the `/admin/migrations` run/retry dialog is the reference pattern. Never wire a destructive `onClick` straight to `action.submit(...)`, and do not use `window.confirm` for new code.

## Shared constants, not inline literals

Tunable constants (page sizes, limits, polling intervals, thresholds) live in a shared `src/lib` module and are imported where needed — `lib/pagination.ts` is the reference pattern for page sizes. Do not declare `const PAGE_SIZE = 25` (or similar) inside a page/component/hook; add it to the appropriate shared file (or create one per concern) and import it. One shared definition means one place to tune the value app-wide.

## Styling

Tailwind v4 utility classes plus the CSS variables from `@questorylabs/ui/styles.css` (`--ink`, `--accent`, fonts), imported by `globals.css`. No new CSS modules (the only existing ones are legacy under `components/enterprise/`), no inline style objects for things Tailwind covers.

## App Router

Routes live under `src/app` with the `(app)`/`(admin)` route groups and their shells. Follow the existing client-component + ResourceStore pattern for pages; do not introduce one-off server-side data fetching patterns without need.
